{
  "description": "The session list's sections and their order, which the web, Apple and Android clients each test against. Server: session.listed_at (migration 1434, src/apiserver/src/sessions/session-listed-at.ts). Each row's serverFacts are the columns the server holds for it (docs/session-status-retirement-plan.md section 2.6); its status is the legacy wire word derived from them, which is what a client reads: no client reads serverFacts, and the server spec reads only them.",
  "rule": [
    "Input: the Open list's rows. A row with completedAt or deletedAt set is not in it (the Completed view orders by completedAt; Trash is its own view).",
    "Each row goes to the FIRST section that takes it, in this order: Pinned, Needs you, Working, then one date section.",
    "Pinned: pinnedAt is set.",
    "Needs you: needsOwner, which is pendingApprovals > 0 (a permission card, a question, an owner decision waiting on this row) OR status FAILED with no retryAt armed.",
    "Working: status RUNNING or PENDING, or status FAILED with retryAt armed (the server is retrying it).",
    "Every other row goes to a date section by the calendar day of listedAt (createdAt when listedAt is null), counted back from today in the reader's time zone: 0 or a future instant 'Today', 1 'Yesterday', 2–7 '2–7 days ago', 8–30 '8–30 days ago', more 'Older'.",
    "Within every section: listedAt descending (createdAt when null), then createdAt descending, then id ascending. lastTurnAt is never an order key: it is the liveness clock and moves with every streamed event.",
    "Empty sections are not drawn.",
    "listedAt moves only when the session changes for its owner: it is created; a person sends it a message; a turn ends on the owner (a person's turn answered, a card or question raised, an owner request filed); it ends (SUCCEEDED, FAILED, CANCELLED) or is completed. Streamed text, tool calls, background-job output, wake-up turns, queue claims and runner reconnects do not move it."
  ],
